Original commit body from ff911ae7d2203d8590e699f0790ec1253ff4219b:

_extract_phoenix_routes walked every call in every file and minted a
route marker for any get/post/put/patch/delete/head/options/resources/
live call whose first positional argument was a string. Two families of
plain calls matched: a cache module's own get("user_#{id}") and a
Phoenix.ConnTest request conn |> get("/pages") in a test (the pipe
supplies the conn, so the path becomes argument 0).

_iter_router_calls now yields only calls lexically inside a defmodule
whose top-level body runs `use Phoenix.Router`, the generated web-module
dispatcher `use AppWeb, :router` (its def router quotes use
Phoenix.Router, so the :router atom is the evidence and the web module
itself is no router), or `use Plug.Router`. A Plug.Router module mints
the HTTP verbs only (Plug.Router has no resources/live). A nested
defmodule starts afresh. A call on the right of |> is never a route
macro, inside a router too (a piped get in a router's plug function is a
request helper; a route macro taking the conn as its path would not
compile).

Test fixtures that declared routes in a module with no `use` (which
would not compile under Phoenix) now carry `use Phoenix.Router` /
`use MyAppWeb, :router`.

thc: 738 Phoenix route symbols (377 router.ex, 348 test, 13 lib cache)
-> 377, all router.ex, identical names/lines/controllers/actions.

